# Moto G20 (java): enforcing system-boot rules.
# Harvested from the first enforcing boot (OTA f348e3d6, 2026-10-03): the
# boot stalled at bootlogo on two crash-looping HALs - hangdiag recorded
# HDST tmo=45 at 88s uptime and ramoops held all 28 avc denials, all three
# patterns below. Scoped to the non-recovery policy: the HAL types are not
# declared in the recovery policy build (sepolicy.recovery).

ifelse(target_recovery, `true', , `
# Boot control HAL (vendor.sprd.boot-hal-1-1): by-name/misc resolves to a
# node labeled block_device in the merged contexts (the stock vendor
# mmcblk_device labeling never applies here), so the stock grant misses and
# the HAL exited status 1 in a one-per-second restart loop, taking slot
# logic (and the boot) with it. Slot ops need the full rw set.
allow hal_bootctrl_default block_device:blk_file { ioctl read write getattr open };

# The same HAL probes /metadata/gsi (Virtual A/B) during init.
allow hal_bootctrl_default gsi_metadata_file:dir search;

# Unisoc keymaster reaches Trusty through trusty-ipc-dev0, labeled generic
# device in our merged contexts. Without read/write the HAL never
# registered and hwservicemanager looped on ctl.interface_start.
allow hal_keymaster_unisoc device:chr_file { ioctl read write getattr open };
')
